      passage: "I have a pet rabbit. Her name is Coco, and she is three years old. She is white with brown ears and a small pink nose. She is very soft, and she has a short, round tail.\n\nCoco lives in a big wooden house in our garden. In winter, when it's very cold, she lives inside our house, in the kitchen.\n\nEvery morning before school, I give Coco fresh water and food. Rabbits eat a lot of hay — that's dry grass. Coco also loves carrots, apples and green vegetables. But she can't eat chocolate or bread, because they are bad for rabbits.\n\nAfter school, I play with Coco in the garden. She runs and jumps very fast. When she is happy, she jumps in the air and turns around. It's very funny!\n\nOn Saturdays, I clean her house. It takes about thirty minutes. It's not my favourite job, but Coco needs a clean home.\n\nRabbits are good pets, but they need a lot of time and love. Coco is very friendly. Now she sits next to me when I read in the garden.",
