      title: "Four Seasons in My Country",
      passage: "Hi, I'm Elif, and I live in Ankara, the capital of Turkey. In my country, we have four seasons, and every season is different. Which season do I like best? Read and see!\n\nSpring is from March to May. The weather is warm, and there are flowers everywhere. On sunny weekends, my family and I have picnics in the park. My mum loves spring.\n\nSummer is from June to August. It's very hot and dry in Ankara — sometimes thirty-five degrees! There's no school, so we go to my grandparents' house near the sea. I swim every day and eat a lot of watermelon.\n\nAutumn is from September to November. The leaves on the trees are yellow, orange and red. It's often windy, and it starts to rain. School starts again in September. My dad likes autumn because he likes walking in the forest.\n\nWinter is from December to February. It's cold, and it often snows in Ankara. My brother and I make snowmen and drink hot chocolate.\n\nMy favourite season is winter, because I love snow — and because my birthday is in January!",
